ber 16, 2016\n\nEssay Length: 5,540 Words / 23 Pages\n\nPaper type: Research Paper\n\nViews: 1,285--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHealthcare System Components Essays and Term Papers 1 - 25 (https://www.essaysforstudent.com/topics/Healthcare%2BSystem%2BComponents/page1.html)\nciteturn11search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.2 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; Essay Length: 853 Words / 4 Pages ... AdaptCache: Adaptive Data Partitioning for Distributed Object Caches Omar Asad School of Computer Science McGill University Montreal, Canada oasad@cs.mcgill.ca Supervised By: Bettina Kemme Abstract—This paper presents AdaptCache, an adaptive data management system for key-value cache stores.\nRating:\n\nEssay Length: 853 Words / 4 Pages\n\nSubmitted: January 24, 2010 By: Mike\n\nAccess this essay Save\n\n  * ## Adaptability and Caching in Component-Based System Environment\n\nAdaptCache: Adaptive Data Partitioning for Distributed Object Caches Omar Asad School of Computer Science McGill University Montreal, Canada oasad@cs.mcgill.ca Supervised By: Bettina Kemme Abstract—This paper presents AdaptCache, an adaptive data management system for key-value cache stores. AdaptCache is a lightweight library that is capable of receiving live workload information from different caches and, based on predefined caching solutions, generate policies to rearrange client requests as well as their respective objects among caches in a way\n\nRating:\n\nEssay Length: 5,540 Words / 23 Pages\n\nSubmitted: October 16, 2016 By: omarasad\n\nAccess this essay Save\n\n  * ## Computer Operating System\n\nIntroduction An operating system (OS) is a program that acts an intermediary between a user of a computer and the computer hardware. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAdaptCache: Adaptive Data Partitioning and Migration for Distributed Object Caches | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/309961421_AdaptCache_Adaptive_Data_Partitioning_and_Migration_for_Distributed_Object_Caches)\nciteturn11search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; # AdaptCache: Adaptive Data Partitioning and Migration for Distributed Object Caches ... Bettina Kemme\n\n# AdaptCache: Adaptive Data Partitioning and Migration for Distributed Object Caches\n\n  * November 2016\n\nDOI:10.1145/2988336.2988343\n\n  * Conference: the 17th International Middleware Conference\n\nAuthors:\n\nOmar Asad\n\n  * McGill University\n\nBettina Kemme\n\nBettina Kemme\n\n## Abstract\n\nCaching is an important aspect of today's web enterprise systems, enhancing performance and reducing access frequency to the backend storage server. However, when implemented as an independent component, such as when using Memcached, access to the remote cache can lead to considerable overhead and delay. Instead, in this paper we propose a cooperative and integrated cache framework where each application server has its own local cache but can also access the caches of other servers. Our solution dynamically distributes objects across caches and requests across servers such that the load is equally distributed across servers and servers find the objects they need for request execution in their local cache most of the time. The challenge is to handle the complex workloads of current e-commerce sites where requests can access more than one object and change the object set they access over time, and different request types access overlapping sets of objects. As such, we look at a whole range of distribution mechanisms and analyze their behavior in detail. We evaluated the various alternatives using the YCSB and RUBiS benchmarks, showing that our approach is applicable in different dynamic workload scenarios and is able to autonomously capture workload changes and adapt instantly.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndblp: AdaptCache: Adaptive Data Partitioning and Migration for Distributed Object Caches. (https://dblp.org/rec/conf/middleware/AsadK16.html)\nciteturn11search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.9 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; # \"AdaptCache: Adaptive Data Partitioning and Migration for Distributed ...\" ... Omar Asad, Bettina Kemme (2016) ... AdaptCache: Adaptive Data Partitioning and Migration for Distributed Object Caches.\n\n# \"AdaptCache: Adaptive Data Partitioning and Migration for Distributed ...\"\n\n  * help us\n\n    * How can I correct errors in dblp?\n    * contact dblp\n\nOmar Asad, Bettina Kemme (2016)\n\n  *   * Image: use mirror server\n\nDagstuhl\n\n  * Trier\n\n  * > Home\n\n## Details and statistics\n\nDOI: —\n\naccess: closed\n\ntype: Conference or Workshop Paper\n\nmetadata version: 2016-11-15\n\n    * view\n\n      * electronic edition @ acm.org\n \n\n    * export record\n\n      * BibTeX\n      * RIS\n      * RDF N-Triples\n      * RDF Turtle\n      * RDF/XML\n      * XML\n      * plain text\n\ndblp key:\n\n      * conf/middleware/AsadK16\n\n\n      * https://dblp.org/rec/conf/middleware/AsadK16\n\nOmar Asad, Bettina Kemme:\nAdaptCache: Adaptive Data Partitioning and Migration for Distributed Object Caches. Middleware 2016: 7\n\n\nlast updated on 2016-11-15 15:07 CET by the dblp team\n\n all metadata released as open data under CC0 1.0 license--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPROADAPT: Proactive framework for adaptive partitioning for big data warehouses - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0169023X22000933)\nciteturn11search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; To solve such limitations, we propose in this paper a proactive framework for query-aware adaptive partitioning (called PROADAPT) that uses an AI-inspired methodology that can be connected to any query optimizer managing partitioned data. ... Kemme, Adaptcache: Adaptive data partitioning and migration for distributed object caches, in: Proceedings...\n\n